- The eight characters are ten bytes in UTF-8, since each accented letter takes two.
- [Characters](characters.md) covers encodings, and [Base encoding](base-encoding.md) writes bytes
- as hexadecimal or Base64 text.
+ Los ocho caracteres son diez bytes en UTF-8, ya que cada letra acentuada ocupa dos.
+ [Caracteres](characters.md) trata las codificaciones, y [Codificación en base](base-encoding.md)
+ escribe bytes como texto hexadecimal o Base64.

- ### Fuzzy matching
+ ### Comparación aproximada

- Two pieces of text can be compared for closeness, not just equality, through a `Proximity`
- measure in scope. The [Levenshtein](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levenshtein_distance) distance
- counts the single-character edits between them:
+ Dos trozos de texto se pueden comparar por su cercanía, no solo por su igualdad, mediante una
+ medida de `Proximity` en el ámbito. La distancia de
+ [Levenshtein](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Levenshtein_distance) cuenta las ediciones de un
+ solo carácter que hay entre ellos:

= counts the single-character edits between them:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- import proximities.levenshteinProximity
+ import proximities.levenshteinProximity

- import caseSensitivity.caseSensitive
+ import caseSensitivity.caseSensitive

= import caseSensitivity.caseSensitive
- ```
+ ```

